# Music from elsewhere in the room: another device plays it, so the
# machine's echo canceller knows nothing of it. The name listener hears
# its start, and once that brought no words takes it for a background,
# which does not keep the recogniser busy; when the music stops, so does
# the background (music starting again is listened to again); and calling
# the agent over it still wakes it.
agent-asleep
fail-on "PANIC"
wait-serial "desktop ready" 120
mic-silence 2
wait-serial "listening for its name" 30
# The music starts: listened to, and a background once eight seconds
# brought no words.
mic-music "Neon Horizon" -6
wait-serial "someone is speaking" 20
wait-serial "sound without words; listening for its name over it" 20
# It stops for longer than a pause between songs: so does the background.
mic-music off
wait-serial "the sound without words stopped" 15
# It starts again: listened to again, a background again.
checkpoint
mic-music "Neon Horizon" -6
wait-serial "someone is speaking" 20
wait-serial "sound without words; listening for its name over it" 20
wait 20
# Over it, only what stands out is listened to: its two starts, and once
# maybe as it grows louder than its quiet beginning.
agent-listens-at-most 3
agent-not-listening 20
checkpoint
mic-tone 2 16000
wait-serial "someone is speaking" 20
agent-hear "Hey Veda, stop the music." 30
wait-serial "woken by its name" 20
agent-connected 60
agent-expect "Hey Veda, stop the music." 20
